-- title:
--   Invariance upgrade for natural Γ̃-equivariant families on nilpotent algebras
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring with irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and with fraction field $K_0$; let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a characteristic-zero $\mathcal O$-domain with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$. Further data: a homomorphism $v_{\det}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively), a group $G$, a $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0\colon \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$, a subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of the unit group of the quaternion algebra with a homomorphism $\theta_t\colon\Gamma_t\to G$, a scheme $T$ with a morphism $t$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, and, for each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map $\rho'_B$ from $\bigl((O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}(\pi,B)\bigr)\times G$ to the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to T$ over $t$. Two properties of $\rho'$ are assumed: naturality in $B$ along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hρnat`), and invariance (`hρinv`): for $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, $g\in G$ and points $x,x'$ of $(O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\mathrm{DeligneDatum}$ with $x'$ obtained from $x$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ — that is, $x'_1=x_1\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-v_{\det}(\iota_0\gamma)}$ and, for every full lattice $M$, the line of $x'_2$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $x_2$ at $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}M$ under the base-changed action of $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ — one has $\rho'_B(x',\theta_t(\gamma)g)=\rho'_B(x,g)$. The conclusion: for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent, all $x_1,x_2\in\bigl((O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}C)\times\mathrm{DeligneDatum}(\pi,C)\bigr)\times G$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$, if (i) the Deligne datum components satisfy the pullback relation for $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, namely for every full lattice $M$ the line of $x_{2}$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $x_{1}$ at $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}M$; (ii) the two $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to C$ given by $x_2$ and by $x_1\circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v_{\det}(\iota_0\gamma)}$ agree merely on those $y\in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{v_{\det}(\iota_0 z)}$ for every $z\in\Gamma_t$ that is a rational scalar in the quaternion algebra and lies in the kernel of $\theta_t$; and (iii) the $G$-components satisfy $x_{2}=\theta_t(\gamma)\,x_{1}$, then $\rho'_C(x_2)=\rho'_C(x_1)$.
--
--   This is the step, in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the fake-elliptic-curve moduli problem, that upgrades the $\tilde\Gamma$-invariance hypothesis on a natural family $\rho'$ on $\pi$-nilpotent algebras: agreement of the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-components only on the elements fixed by the relevant Frobenius powers already forces equal values, the gap being bridged by the uniqueness of factorisations through the fixed points of $\mathrm{Fr}$ and by the triviality of the action of scalar matrices on Deligne data. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_apply_eq_apply_of_isPullback_of_frobTwist_eq_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_apply_eq_apply_of_isPullback_of_frobTwist_eq_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_eq).
